WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
我们也是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.020
Hi, Angela.
嗨，安吉拉。

9
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.440
Hi there, lady.
嗨，女士。

10
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:26.720
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

11
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:27.560
Hi.
嗨。

12
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.240
Today, we're going to talk about the cover-up.
今天，我们要聊聊《掩盖》这一集。

13
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:36.040
It is Season 6, Episode 24, written by Gene Stepnitzky and Lee Eisenberg.
这是第六季第24集，由吉恩·斯蒂普尼茨基和李·艾森伯格编剧。

14
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:36.680
We love them.
我们很喜欢他们。

15
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.280
And directed by our very own Rainn Wilson.
由我们自己的雷恩·威尔森执导。

16
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:40.300
Rainn!
雷恩！

17
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.120
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

18
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:50.400
Michael becomes convinced that Donna, remember the manager from Sid and Dexter's, who bought all the printers last week.
迈克尔确信唐娜——还记得那位来自“希德与德克斯特”的经理吗？她上周买走了所有的打印机。

19
00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:51.700
How many we don't know.
具体买了多少我们不知道。

20
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.240
How many she needs, we're not sure.
她需要多少我们也不确定。

21
00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.780
But it turns out Michael was right.
但事实证明迈克尔是对的。

22
00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.280
She was giving signals they are full-on dating.
她当时发出的信号表明他们正在全面约会。

23
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.680
But today, he's going to become convinced that Donna is cheating on him.
但今天，他开始确信唐娜在背着他偷情。

24
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:05.720
Yes.
没错。

25
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.680
And he's going to ask Dwight to find out the truth.
他打算让德怀特去查明真相。

26
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.700
I mean, this is Dwight's Super Bowl.
我是说，这简直是德怀特的“超级碗”。

27
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.240
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

28
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:14.020
He's so excited.
他真的太兴奋了。

29
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.300
He gets to go undercover.
他终于可以去卧底了。

30
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.320
I mean, he, like, dives across a table in the break room when he gets the news.
我是说，当他听到这个消息时，他直接从休息室的桌子上扑了过去。

31
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.640
That wasn't even in the script.
那甚至都不在剧本里。

32
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.240
I wanted to see.
我想确认一下。

33
00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:24.640
I looked it up in the shooting draft.
我查了拍摄剧本。

34
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.660
It just says, Dwight sprints out.
上面只写着，德怀特冲了出去。

35
00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.940
But that table move?
但那个翻桌子的动作？

36
00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:28.840
That was Rain.
那是雷恩自己加的。

37
00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.140
I believe it.
我相信。

38
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:37.020
Well, meanwhile, Daryl gets delayed revenge on Andy for a past issue that upset him.
与此同时，达里尔因为一件让他心烦的往事，对安迪展开了迟来的报复。

39
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:44.980
And he does this by making him think that Gabe is going to fire him for revealing the truth about the faulty saber printers.
他让安迪以为盖博要因为他揭露了“赛博”打印机故障的真相而开除他。

40
00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:49.040
Turns out, sometimes they catch on fire.
事实证明，它们有时真的会着火。

41
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.880
Turns out, there might be something really happening.
看来，可能真的出事了。

42
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:56.980
Fast fact number one is that Rainn Wilson directed this episode.
第一个速览事实是，雷恩·威尔森执导了这一集。

43
00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.720
Rainn directed three episodes of The Office.
雷恩一共执导了三集《办公室》。

44
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.420
And this was his firSt.
而这是他的第一集。

45
00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.880
We reached out to Rainn.
我们联系了雷恩。

46
00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.280
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

47
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.060
And he sent in some audio clips, which he recorded...
他发来了一些音频片段，是他录制的……

48
00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.700
While driving...
在开车的时候……

49
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.620
In traffic.
在堵车的时候。

50
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.280
And you can hear at the end, it's like, accident up ahead.
你可以在最后听到他说，前面有事故。

51
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:18.700
It's like, Rainn, maybe stop talking to us.
就好像是说，雷恩，也许别再跟我们说话了。

52
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:20.520
All right.
好的。

53
00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.980
Here is what Rainn had to say about directing.
以下是雷恩关于导演工作的看法。

54
00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.280
Hello there, office ladies.
你们好啊，办公室女士们。

55
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.320
It's me, your old pal, Rainn.
是我，你们的老朋友，雷恩。

56
00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:33.120
So I understand you're doing the cover-up in this week's episode.
我听说你们这周要聊那集“掩盖真相”。

57
00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:33.940
How exciting.
太令人兴奋了。

58
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:37.760
Dwight unleashed as a private detective to investigate Donna.
德怀特化身为私家侦探去调查唐娜。

59
00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:46.900
A lot of great scenes in the gym with that great ending of Dwight leading the cycling spin class.
健身房里有很多精彩的戏份，最后德怀特带领大家做动感单车课的结尾也很棒。

60
00:02:47.470 --> 00:02:52.940
A lot of people ask about what it's like to act in the show while you're directing.
很多人问我，一边演戏一边当导演是什么感觉。

61
00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.200
You know, the fortunate thing is that we were so familiar with the show at that point.
你知道，幸运的是，那时候我们对这部剧已经非常熟悉了。

62
00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.520
It would have been impossible in the first three seasons.
在前三季里这根本是不可能的。

63
00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.240
Impossible.
不可能。

64
00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:13.180
You know, we're still kind of learning the landscape and still discovering stuff about our characters and, you know, getting used to how everything's going.
你知道，那时候我们还在摸索门道，还在不断发现角色的新东西，还在适应一切的运作方式。

65
00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:18.680
But by season six, here we are, four, five, six, we get the show.
但到了第六季，也就是第四、五、六季的时候，我们已经完全理解这部剧了。

66
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.760
We get how it's shot, where to place cameras.
我们知道它是怎么拍摄的，知道摄像机该放在哪里。

67
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.200
It's a lot easier.
这容易多了。

68
00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:30.960
There's always some scenes that are quite challenging and difficult to figure out how you're going to cover them in a unique and interesting way.
总有一些场景是相当具有挑战性的，很难想出如何以独特且有趣的方式去呈现它们。

69
00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:34.040
The thing I always said about the directing of The Office is, like,
关于《办公室》的导演工作，我一直以来的看法是，

70
00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:43.300
the scripts are so good and the cast is so good and the camera crew is so good that you'll always get at least a B-plus episode.
剧本太棒了，演员阵容太棒了，摄影团队也太棒了，所以你总能拍出一集至少是B+水准的剧集。

71
00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:54.400
So, what the really good directors like Ken Quapas and Paul Feig and several others were able to do is, like, take a B-plus, A-minus episode and move it to an A.
所以，像肯·夸皮斯、保罗·费格和其他几位真正优秀的导演所能做的，就是把一集B+或A-的剧集提升到A的水平。

72
00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:06.240
So, you always want just those little touches, the little flourishes, the little improvs, interesting ways to shoot things, can kind of just raise the level a little bit.
所以，你总是希望加入一些小点缀、小花样、小即兴，以及有趣的拍摄手法，这样就能把水平稍微提高一点。

73
00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.560
And that's kind of always the goal as a director.
作为导演，这始终是目标所在。

74
00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.800
I think Paul Lieberstein was an excellent director for The Office.
我认为保罗·利伯斯坦是《办公室》的一位优秀导演。

75
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:15.320
He really got that, captured a lot of subtlety in the show.
他真的抓住了精髓，捕捉到了剧中许多微妙之处。

76
00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:22.060
And what an amazing bounty for all of us to kind of flex our directing muscles and get an opportunity to direct.
能有机会锻炼我们的导演能力，这对于我们所有人来说都是一份了不起的馈赠。

77
00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:24.000
I learned so much.
我学到了很多。

78
00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:33.500
You know, it keeps coming up again and again with our directors, whether established or new, how great our crew and how supportive our crew was.
你知道，我们的导演们——无论是资深的还是新晋的——总是不断提到我们的团队有多棒，有多么支持我们。

79
00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.660
And what a well-oiled machine we were at this point.
而且我们当时已经是一台运转良好的机器了。

80
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.880
I mean, Rain's really right.
我是说，雷恩说得真对。

81
00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:37.400
Yeah.
没错。

82
00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:39.940
And we also really knew our characters.
而且我们也确实非常了解自己的角色。

83
00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.920
Well, I also asked Rain, what was challenging about directing?
嗯，我还问了雷恩，导演工作有什么挑战？

84
00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:46.780
Here's what he had to say.
以下是他的回答。

85
00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:50.600
It was challenging because, you know, you're working with your castmates.
这很有挑战性，因为你是在和你的搭档们一起工作。

86
00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.640
And these are people that know you as an actor.
他们都是把你当作演员来看待的人。

87
00:04:54.640 --> 00:05:01.740
So, you have to be quite gentle and diplomatic in your notes and in your thoughts because you're working with your family.
所以，你在提意见和想法时必须非常温和且讲究策略，因为你是在和家人一起工作。

88
00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:06.100
You know, you're not all of a sudden Orson Welles, the boss.
你并不是突然变成了奥逊·威尔斯那样的老板。

89
00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:10.360
You're a collaborator offering a point of view on directing the episode.
你只是一个合作者，为导演这一集提供一个视角。

90
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.940
But I found it really fun to kind of put on the director hat and then put on the Dwight hat.
但我发现戴上导演帽，然后再戴上德怀特帽，这种转换真的很有趣。

91
00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:23.240
But like I said, you can only do that if you've been doing it for many, many years and feel really comfortable in your character.
但就像我说的，只有当你已经做了很多很多年，并且对自己的角色感到非常自在时，你才能做到这一点。

92
00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:29.420
You're just able to slip on your character clothes and personality and point of view and jump right in.
你能够直接穿上角色的衣服，进入角色的个性和视角，立刻投入其中。

93
00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.780
Otherwise, it would have been extremely difficult.
否则，这会极其困难。

94
00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:37.240
And we got a lot of support as actors moving into the director's chair.
而且作为演员转型导演，我们得到了很多支持。

95
00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:43.260
It was a delightful episode towards the end of season six and had a blaSt.
那是第六季末尾非常令人愉快的一集，我玩得很开心。

96
00:05:43.260 --> 00:05:45.620
And I'm glad you guys are digging into it.
很高兴你们能深入挖掘这一集。

97
00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:46.340
All right.
好的。

98
00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:47.320
All for now.
暂时就这些。

99
00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.680
Love you guys.
爱你们。

100
00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:49.060
Bye.
再见。

101
00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:57.480
I could imagine it would be really weird to direct people you've been hanging out with for six years.
我能想象，去执导一群相处了六年的朋友，感觉一定很奇怪。

102
00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.000
Oh, for sure.
噢，那肯定的。

103
00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.520
But I loved this quote from what Rain said.
但我很喜欢雷恩说的那句话。

104
00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:07.500
He said he saw himself as a collaborator offering a point of view.
他说他把自己看作是一个提供观点的合作者。

105
00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:11.820
I have to say, I feel like that encapsulates the whole tone of our show.
我不得不说，我觉得这句话概括了我们整部剧的基调。

106
00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.940
We were all collaborators with a point of view.
我们都是有观点的合作者。

107
00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:18.660
And we had this safe place where we could share our point of view.
而且我们拥有一个可以分享彼此观点的安全空间。

108
00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.360
Thank you, Rain, for sending in those audio clips.
谢谢你，雷恩，发来那些音频片段。

109
00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.060
It was very generous of him because he just got back from Iceland.
他真是太慷慨了，因为他刚从冰岛回来。

110
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.020
Yes, he literally just flew back from Iceland.
没错，他真的是刚从冰岛飞回来。

111
00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:31.120
Rain, you brave jet lag to talk to us.
雷恩，你克服了时差来和我们聊天。

112
00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:40.960
What he was doing in Iceland is a new television show called The Geography of Bliss, One Grump's Search for the Happiest Places in the World.
他在冰岛做的是一档名为《幸福地理学：一个怪脾气的人对世界上最幸福地方的探索》的新电视节目。

113
00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:42.840
I cannot wait.
我等不及要看了。

114
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.180
I cannot believe this job.
我简直不敢相信这份工作。

115
00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:46.900
How do you get this job?
你是怎么得到这份工作的？

116
00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:48.580
I mean, Jenna, how?
我是说，珍娜，怎么做到的？

117
00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.320
It's just like the coolest thing.
这简直是最酷的事情了。

118
00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.620
He gets to travel all over and just be himself.
他可以到处旅行，做回他自己。

119
00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:57.320
Yeah, he gets to go to Iceland, Ghana, Japan, and more.
是啊，他可以去冰岛、加纳、日本等等地方。

120
00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:05.680
And it says it's a six-part travel series where he will try to discover how changing your location and perspective can change your life.
上面说这是一个六集的旅行系列节目，他将尝试探索改变地点和视角如何改变你的生活。

121
00:07:06.140 --> 00:07:07.940
This is the greatest job of all time.
这是史上最棒的工作。

122
00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:08.560
It's so awesome, Rain.
太赞了，雷恩。

123
00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:09.700
Why didn't we think of this?
我们怎么就没想到呢？

124
00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.440
Rain, we cannot wait to watch.
雷恩，我们迫不及待想看了。

125
00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:18.900
Can me and you do The Geography of Bliss Part 2 to Ladies Who Love Factories?
我和你能不能做《幸福地理学》第二部，叫《爱工厂的女士们》？

126
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:19.520
Yes.
好啊。

127
00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.440
Can we do that?
我们能做吗？

128
00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:22.520
Can it just be Ladies Who Love Factories?
能不能就叫《爱工厂的女士们》？

129
00:07:22.900 --> 00:07:25.260
We'll just travel the United States.
我们就去美国各地旅行。

130
00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:27.060
We don't even have to go far.
甚至都不用去太远的地方。

131
00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.100
I like this show.
我喜欢这个节目。

132
00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.300
I really like it.
我真的很喜欢。

133
00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.780
Call us, anyone who makes shows.
给我们打电话吧，任何制作节目的人。

134
00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:33.280
Anybody.
任何人都可以。

135
00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:34.960
All right.
好吧。

136
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:42.600
And fast fact number two, this show centers around Michael's suspicion that Donna is cheating on him.
第二个冷知识，这一集围绕着迈克尔怀疑唐娜出轨展开。

137
00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.140
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

138
00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:44.960
So guess what I Googled?
所以你猜我谷歌了什么？

139
00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:46.620
Wait.
等等。

140
00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.760
Sign someone's cheating?
有人出轨的迹象？

141
00:07:50.420 --> 00:07:51.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

142
00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:51.840
Yes.
没错。

143
00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:52.360
Really?
真的吗？

144
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.360
Literally.
千真万确。

145
00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.200
Signs someone is cheating.
有人出轨的迹象。

146
