00:28:25.080 --> 00:28:29.560
This was a whole runner in Secretary's Day towards the end of the episode when people
这是《秘书节》那集快结束时的一个贯穿始终的梗，当时大家

654
00:28:29.560 --> 00:28:30.900
are trying to comfort Aaron.
都在试图安慰艾琳。

655
00:28:31.360 --> 00:28:33.720
This is Ryan and Kelly's way of comforting her.
这是瑞安和凯莉安慰她的方式。

656
00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:34.880
You did not share.
你没分享。

657
00:28:35.040 --> 00:28:35.920
I didn't share.
我没分享。

658
00:28:35.980 --> 00:28:37.140
That is news to me.
这对我来说可是新闻。

659
00:28:37.200 --> 00:28:38.460
Well, there you have it.
好吧，事实就是这样。

660
00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:41.320
We had a fan catch from Ray H.
我们收到了来自佛罗里达州杰克逊维尔的雷·H发来的粉丝纠错，

661
00:28:41.420 --> 00:28:44.700
in Jacksonville, Florida, who says, Michael says he and Donna
他说，迈克尔说他和唐娜

662
00:28:44.700 --> 00:28:45.360
went to the P.F.
去了波科诺山的

663
00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:49.060
Chang's in Mount Pocono, but there isn't one in Mount Pocono.
P.F. Chang's餐厅，但波科诺山根本没有那家店。

664
00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:49.860
The nearest P.F.
最近的P.F.

665
00:28:49.900 --> 00:28:53.260
Chang's is in Philadelphia, and it's about an hour and 48 minutes away
Chang's在费城，距离斯克兰顿大约

666
00:28:53.260 --> 00:28:54.060
from Scranton.
一小时四十八分钟车程。

667
00:28:54.260 --> 00:28:59.780
And now here is my other audio clip about how people say things.
现在播放我另一个关于人们说话方式的音频片段。

668
00:29:00.020 --> 00:29:00.460
Oh.
哦。

669
00:29:00.880 --> 00:29:03.260
We got a fan catch from Julia T.
我们收到了来自加利福尼亚州奥兰治的朱莉娅·T发来的粉丝纠错，

670
00:29:03.340 --> 00:29:08.040
in Orange, California, who says, okay, I have become the
她说，好吧，我已经成了

671
00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:08.980
rum tracker.
“房间”发音追踪者了。

672
00:29:10.040 --> 00:29:14.300
All of the Massachusetts people say rum instead of room.
所有马萨诸塞州的人都把“房间”（room）说成“朗姆”（rum）。

673
00:29:14.860 --> 00:29:20.840
John, Steve, Mindy, and BJ, and we hear a big old rum from Ryan in his talking head.
约翰、史蒂夫、敏迪和BJ，我们在瑞安的个人采访里听到了一个大大的“朗姆”。

674
00:29:21.180 --> 00:29:21.960
Here it is.
就是这个。

675
00:29:22.640 --> 00:29:24.680
Does she keep her phone locked around you, Michael?
她和你在一起时会锁手机吗，迈克尔？

676
00:29:24.920 --> 00:29:27.200
Does she watch how much she drinks around you, Michael?
她和你在一起时会注意喝酒的量吗，迈克尔？

677
00:29:27.440 --> 00:29:29.380
Does she leave the rum when she takes phone calls?
她接电话时会离开“朗姆”吗？

678
00:29:29.820 --> 00:29:30.480
There it is.
就是这个。

679
00:29:30.540 --> 00:29:31.120
Did you hear it?
你听到了吗？

680
00:29:31.240 --> 00:29:32.180
Does she leave the rum?
她会离开“朗姆”吗？

681
00:29:32.540 --> 00:29:32.940
Rum.
朗姆。

682
00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:34.440
That's such a fun catch.
这真是个有趣的发现。

683
00:29:34.540 --> 00:29:34.980
I love it.
我喜欢。

684
00:29:34.980 --> 00:29:38.740
So here's what Ryan is talking about in this conference room meeting.
所以这就是瑞安在会议室会议里提到的内容。

685
00:29:39.060 --> 00:29:43.500
Everyone starts wondering, like, why do you have to go to these weird places to be with
每个人都开始纳闷，为什么你非得去那些奇怪的地方

686
00:29:43.500 --> 00:29:44.060
your girlfriend?
和你女朋友待在一起？

687
00:29:44.340 --> 00:29:45.520
Is she avoiding someone?
她在躲着谁吗？

688
00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:46.820
Is she cheating on you?
她在背着你偷情吗？

689
00:29:47.040 --> 00:29:49.680
Kelly is the first person to pick up on this.
凯莉是第一个察觉到这一点的人。

690
00:29:49.880 --> 00:29:51.720
Kelly says, why'd you go to that one?
凯莉说，你为什么要选那一家？

691
00:29:51.780 --> 00:29:52.720
It's so far.
太远了。

692
00:29:53.260 --> 00:29:56.540
And then she's like, Ryan used to do that to me.
然后她说，瑞安以前也对我这样。

693
00:29:56.920 --> 00:29:57.240
Yeah.
是啊。

694
00:29:57.660 --> 00:29:57.960
Yeah.
是啊。

695
00:29:58.420 --> 00:30:01.900
Pam tries to be a voice of reason, but by the end of this conference room meeting,
帕姆试图保持理智，但到这次会议室会议结束时，

696
00:30:01.900 --> 00:30:04.640
Michael is now convinced that Donna is cheating on him.
迈克尔已经认定唐娜在背着他偷情了。

697
00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:05.120
Yeah.
是啊。

698
00:30:05.340 --> 00:30:06.300
It happens so quickly.
发生得太快了。

699
00:30:06.980 --> 00:30:07.360
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

700
00:30:07.600 --> 00:30:11.060
Pam says, Michael, do not let your imagination run out of control.
帕姆说，迈克尔，别让你的想象力失控了。

701
00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:13.700
Michael says, well, that's easy for you to say.
迈克尔说，好吧，你说得倒轻松。

702
00:30:13.840 --> 00:30:15.080
You have a bad imagination.
你的想象力太匮乏了。

703
00:30:15.280 --> 00:30:16.020
It's stupid.
这太蠢了。

704
00:30:16.240 --> 00:30:17.920
I live in a fantasy world.
我活在幻想世界里。

705
00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:25.520
Now Michael is going to do something that he should know better.
现在迈克尔要做一件他本该知道不该做的事。

706
00:30:25.920 --> 00:30:27.000
Oh, Michael, Michael.
噢，迈克尔，迈克尔。

707
00:30:27.200 --> 00:30:28.600
He is going to go in the break room.
他要走进休息室了。

708
00:30:28.740 --> 00:30:31.600
And I titled this scene, Whispers in the Break Room.
我给这一幕起名叫“休息室里的耳语”。

709
00:30:32.160 --> 00:30:35.220
Anyone want to write a song called Whispers in the Break Room?
有人想写一首叫《休息室里的耳语》的歌吗？

710
00:30:35.880 --> 00:30:41.340
He goes up to Dwight and gets like in his ear, so much so that Dwight's like,
他走到德怀特身边，凑到他耳边，凑得太近了，以至于德怀特反应是，

711
00:30:41.460 --> 00:30:43.060
what are you doing?
你在干什么？

712
00:30:43.580 --> 00:30:47.540
And he whispers, I want someone to follow Donna.
然后他耳语道，我想让人跟踪唐娜。

713
00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:48.900
I want her tailed.
我要让人盯着她。

714
00:30:49.060 --> 00:30:51.680
I need the name of a good private investigator.
我需要一个好的私家侦探的名字。

715
00:30:53.180 --> 00:30:57.520
And Dwight is going to give Michael his business card with rates.
德怀特打算把印有收费标准的个人名片给迈克尔。

716
00:30:58.520 --> 00:30:59.880
This scene was longer.
这一幕原本更长。

717
00:30:59.880 --> 00:31:03.920
It was in the shooting draft, and this is how good our scripts come in.
它出现在拍摄剧本里，我们的剧本写得有多好由此可见一斑。

718
00:31:04.040 --> 00:31:08.920
As I was reading the shooting draft, I started laughing out loud just because this is so absurd.
当我读到拍摄剧本时，我忍不住大笑起来，因为这实在太荒谬了。

719
00:31:09.080 --> 00:31:09.640
Listen to this.
听听这个。

720
00:31:09.960 --> 00:31:10.740
I have to share it.
我必须分享一下。

721
00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:13.580
Dwight goes through his wallet, removes a card.
德怀特翻开钱包，拿出一张名片。

722
00:31:13.820 --> 00:31:15.320
Michael, this is you.
迈克尔，这是你啊。

723
00:31:15.540 --> 00:31:17.160
Dwight smiles to camera proud.
德怀特自豪地对着镜头微笑。

724
00:31:17.680 --> 00:31:18.680
Yes, it is.
没错，就是我。

725
00:31:18.840 --> 00:31:20.060
I used your card, guy.
我用了你的名片，伙计。

726
00:31:20.560 --> 00:31:22.840
Michael, Wade, is he still at the mall?
迈克尔，韦德，他还在商场吗？

727
00:31:24.440 --> 00:31:26.580
Dwight, he doesn't have a kiosk anymore.
德怀特，他不再有摊位了。

728
00:31:26.780 --> 00:31:28.300
He's just working out of the food court.
他现在就在美食广场办公。

729
00:31:28.300 --> 00:31:30.160
Michael, well, what do you charge?
迈克尔，好吧，你收费多少？

730
00:31:30.560 --> 00:31:37.360
It's just, then they can, but I love that he's like, Wade, in the food court, you know, the card guy.
这只是，然后他们可以，但我喜欢他那种感觉，韦德，在美食广场，你知道，那个卖名片的家伙。

731
00:31:37.900 --> 00:31:42.240
I love it that Dwight says that he charges $100 a day plus expenses.
我喜欢德怀特说他每天收费100美元外加开销这一点。

732
00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:44.160
Michael says he'll give him 50.
迈克尔说他只给50。

733
00:31:44.340 --> 00:31:45.120
Money is no object.
钱不是问题。

734
00:31:45.580 --> 00:31:46.200
I know.
我知道。

735
00:31:47.040 --> 00:31:49.920
Then, of course, Dwight's going to scooch you across the table.
然后，当然，德怀特会滑过桌子凑向你。

736
00:31:50.080 --> 00:31:50.600
He's on it.
他干劲十足。

737
00:31:50.760 --> 00:31:51.060
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

738
00:31:51.420 --> 00:31:52.520
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

739
00:31:52.520 --> 00:31:59.780
Well, Jenna, in the episode now, Andy is going to get a call about a printer that caught on fire.
好吧，珍娜，在现在的剧集里，安迪会接到一个关于打印机起火的电话。

740
00:32:00.040 --> 00:32:00.180
Yeah.
是的。

741
00:32:00.860 --> 00:32:08.000
In the shooting draft, after Andy gets the phone call, rather than turning to Stanley or Gabe, the first person he goes to is Kelly.
在拍摄剧本中，安迪接到电话后，他没有转向斯坦利或盖博，而是第一个去找了凯莉。

742
00:32:08.520 --> 00:32:08.920
Oh.
噢。

743
00:32:09.120 --> 00:32:09.500
Yes.
是的。

744
00:32:09.600 --> 00:32:14.600
He wants to know if a client has called customer service complaining about faulty printers.
他想知道是否有客户打电话给客服投诉打印机故障。

745
00:32:14.860 --> 00:32:15.420
Makes sense.
说得通。

746
00:32:15.420 --> 00:32:20.380
We learn a lot about Kelly's attention to detail in this scene, and I thought we should hear it.
我们在这一幕中了解了很多关于凯莉对细节的关注，我觉得我们应该听听看。

747
00:32:20.500 --> 00:32:20.860
All right.
好的。

748
00:32:21.420 --> 00:32:25.760
Hey, Kelly, have you been getting any calls about the Sabre GH400 printers?
嘿，凯莉，你有没有接到关于Sabre GH400打印机的电话？

749
00:32:26.360 --> 00:32:27.220
Yeah, people hate them.
有啊，大家都很讨厌它们。

750
00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:27.660
Really?
真的吗？

751
00:32:27.860 --> 00:32:30.180
Has anyone said that they, like, blow up or anything?
有人说过它们会爆炸之类的吗？

752
00:32:30.600 --> 00:32:31.260
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

753
00:32:31.620 --> 00:32:32.400
Can you check?
你能查一下吗？

754
00:32:32.820 --> 00:32:33.260
Where?
去哪查？

755
00:32:34.880 --> 00:32:35.760
Your records.
你的记录里。

756
00:32:36.140 --> 00:32:38.100
Okay, I don't keep records, per se.
好吧，我其实没留什么记录。

757
00:32:38.260 --> 00:32:40.020
Well, like, in your files, whatever.
就是，你的档案里，随便哪里都行。

758
00:32:40.320 --> 00:32:40.560
Hmm.
嗯。

759
00:32:41.840 --> 00:32:42.540
This would be...
这应该是……

760
00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:43.460
Those are empty.
那些都是空的。

761
00:32:44.640 --> 00:32:45.980
How do you do your job?
那你平时怎么工作？

762
00:32:49.900 --> 00:32:54.800
You know the bank of file cabinets next to her desk we see in all the episodes?
你知道我们每集都能看到她桌子旁边的那排文件柜吗？

763
00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:55.160
Yes.
知道。

764
00:32:55.160 --> 00:32:55.820
They're empty.
它们是空的。

765
00:32:56.060 --> 00:32:57.480
There's nothing in them.
里面什么都没有。

766
00:32:57.680 --> 00:33:00.060
I love that he says, how do you do your job?
我真喜欢他说那句“那你平时怎么工作”。

767
00:33:00.200 --> 00:33:00.660
I know.
我也喜欢。

768
00:33:01.780 --> 00:33:06.120
Lady, do you know that I worked as a customer service representative on a complaint line?
天哪，你们知道我以前在投诉热线做过客服吗？

769
00:33:06.500 --> 00:33:07.120
Oh, no.
噢，不会吧。

770
00:33:07.220 --> 00:33:07.820
How was that?
那份工作怎么样？

771
00:33:08.080 --> 00:33:09.940
It was for a major soda company.
是一家大型汽水公司的。

772
00:33:10.220 --> 00:33:11.240
I won't say which one.
我就不说具体是哪家了。

773
00:33:11.400 --> 00:33:11.980
Can I guess?
我能猜猜吗？

774
00:33:12.360 --> 00:33:14.300
No, I feel like I shouldn't say which one.
不行，我觉得我不该说出是哪家。

775
00:33:14.400 --> 00:33:15.520
Oh, come on!
噢，别这样！

776
00:33:15.520 --> 00:33:16.900
You can guess off-air.
你可以私下猜。

777
00:33:17.200 --> 00:33:18.340
Oh, you guys.
噢，你们这些人。

778
00:33:19.140 --> 00:33:21.500
So, it was my job to sit...
所以，我的工作就是坐在那儿……

779
00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:21.940
Schmapsie?
是“施麦普西”吗？

780
00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:23.220
I'm not going to say.
我不会说的。

781
00:33:23.320 --> 00:33:23.900
Schmuck-a-schmolla?
是“施马克-阿-施莫拉”吗？

782
00:33:24.120 --> 00:33:24.980
I'm not going to say.
我不会说的。

783
00:33:25.140 --> 00:33:25.300
Okay.
好吧。

784
00:33:26.060 --> 00:33:28.360
The best part of the job was that I got free soda.
那份工作最棒的地方就是有免费汽水喝。

785
00:33:28.520 --> 00:33:31.800
They had free fountain sodas in the cafeteria.
餐厅里有免费的汽水机。

786
00:33:32.040 --> 00:33:32.360
Oh.
噢。

787
00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:33.180
It was...
它……

788
00:33:33.180 --> 00:33:33.540
Perks.
福利。

789
00:33:33.620 --> 00:33:37.780
...located in a very kind of remote area, so you couldn't leave at lunchtime.
……位于一个比较偏远的地方，所以午餐时间你没法离开。

790
00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:41.980
Your choices were bring something or go to the cafeteria, but you got free soda.
你只能选择自带午餐或者去餐厅，但你可以喝免费汽水。

791
00:33:41.980 --> 00:33:42.900
All day.
全天供应。

792
00:33:43.180 --> 00:33:44.920
And you worked the complaint line?
那你当时负责投诉热线？

793
00:33:45.060 --> 00:33:52.880
I worked the complaint hotline for two weeks as a temp when the person who normally worked there was on leave.
我做过两周的投诉热线临时工，当时负责那块的人休假去了。

794
00:33:53.060 --> 00:33:53.420
Okay.
好吧。

795
00:33:53.980 --> 00:33:55.520
I had a little bit of training.
我接受过一点点培训。

796
00:33:55.800 --> 00:33:56.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

797
00:33:56.400 --> 00:33:57.720
A little bit of training.
一点点培训。

798
00:33:58.120 --> 00:33:59.180
Like half an hour.
大概半小时吧。

799
00:33:59.460 --> 00:34:00.800
It was like a day.
差不多有一天。

800
00:34:01.040 --> 00:34:02.880
But basically, there was a binder.
但基本上，就是有一本活页夹。

801
00:34:03.140 --> 00:34:11.920
They explained you answer the phone, you listen to the complaint, you take it seriously, you log it, and then you offer to send the person coupons for free soda.
他们解释说，你接听电话，听取投诉，认真对待，做好记录，然后提出给对方寄送免费汽水的优惠券。

802
00:34:12.180 --> 00:34:12.540
Okay.
好的。

803
00:34:12.780 --> 00:34:16.560
As a way to apologize for whatever inconvenience they have had.
作为对他们所遭遇的任何不便表示歉意的一种方式。

804
00:34:16.560 --> 00:34:17.980
And now, did they have a script?
那么，他们有话术脚本吗？

805
00:34:18.060 --> 00:34:22.740
Because you know I worked in telemarketing, and you usually have a script when someone calls to complain that you follow.
因为你知道我做过电话营销，通常有人打电话来投诉时，你得照着脚本说。

806
00:34:22.960 --> 00:34:30.160
There wasn't really a script, but there was a binder that outlined the top complaints and suggested responses.
其实没什么脚本，但有一个活页夹，上面列出了最常见的投诉和建议的回复。

807
00:34:30.420 --> 00:34:30.680
Okay.
好的。

808
00:34:30.680 --> 00:34:39.620
So, for example, the top complaint at the soda company was someone has found a piece of glass or other object in their soda.
比如，汽水公司最常见的投诉是有人发现汽水里有玻璃碎片或其他异物。

809
00:34:39.800 --> 00:34:40.100
Okay.
好的。

810
00:34:40.500 --> 00:34:47.400
And the response to that was our sodas are canned in a glass-free environment.
对此的回复是，我们的汽水是在无玻璃环境下罐装的。

811
00:34:47.780 --> 00:34:56.440
Most likely, the cases were stored next to some kind of broken glass, and then when you opened the soda, it fell in.
最有可能的情况是，箱子存放在某种碎玻璃旁边，当你打开汽水时，玻璃掉进去了。

812
00:34:56.440 --> 00:35:01.320
But there's really no way that we canned it with glass.
但我们绝对不可能在罐装时混入玻璃。

813
